# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TWO connection strings, both required (see docs/DATABASE.md "Connection
# pooling"). On Neon: the dashboard shows both — "Pooled connection" and
# "Direct connection". Get this wrong and either the app can't handle real
# concurrent traffic (missing pooling) or deploys fail (migrations run
# through a pooler that doesn't support them).
#   DATABASE_URL — pooled (PgBouncer). What the running app queries through.
#   DIRECT_URL   — unpooled. What `prisma migrate deploy`/`db push` use.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@ep-example-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&connect_timeout=15"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@ep-example.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require"

# ── Token encryption (Gmail/Drive refresh tokens at rest) ────────────────
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Required before connecting Gmail/Drive — the app refuses to store a
# refresh token without this (see src/lib/crypto.ts).
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── Anthropic (powers every AI Staff agent) ─────────────────────────────
# Without this, the app runs in Demo Mode: agents return clearly-labeled
# canned responses instead of real Claude output. See lib/llm/adapter.ts.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Google OAuth (Gmail + Drive) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) in Google Cloud Console.
# Without these, Integrations → Gmail/Drive show "연결 필요" and the mail
# checker / file organizer agents run in Mock Mode.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/integrations/google/callback

# ── Transcription (meeting audio → text) ────────────────────────────────
# Any provider works behind lib/transcription/adapter.ts; example uses
# a generic key. Without it, Mark only accepts pasted/typed transcripts
# (which always works, no credential needed).
TRANSCRIPTION_API_KEY=

# ── Web search (market-researcher's research tool) ──────────────────────
# Without this, the research tool falls back to a Mock provider that
# returns clearly-labeled placeholder results instead of pretending to
# have searched the live web.
SEARCH_API_KEY=

# ── Auth (not implemented yet — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) ────────────────
# AUTH_SECRET is a placeholder for whenever real login is added. Leave
# AUTH_ENABLED unset/blank — it exists only to turn off the "no login yet"
# warning banner (src/app/layout.tsx) once real auth actually ships. Setting
# it before that just hides a warning that is still true.
AUTH_SECRET=change-me-in-production
AUTH_ENABLED=

# ── Scheduler ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret so only your own cron caller can hit /api/scheduler/tick.
SCHEDULER_SECRET=change-me-in-production
